===Etymology 1===
The {{glossary|verb}} is inherited from {{inh|en|enm|prien}}, {{m|enm|pryen|t=to look closely, peer into, pry, spy}}{{nb...|preien, preye, pri, prie, prihe, prye, pryhe|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=prīen|pos=v|id=MED34607}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|*prīwan}}, {{m|ang|*prēowian|t=to look narrowly, to squint at}}, attested by {{cog|ang|beprīwan}}, {{m|ang|beprēwan|t=to wink}}; further etymology unknown,<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=153665|date=December 2020|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=pry{{sup|1}}|pos=v}}</ref> but probably akin to {{cog|ang|*prēowot|t=closing of the eyes}}, attested only in combination&nbsp;– compare {{m|ang|prēowthwīl|t=blink or twinkling of an eye, moment}}, {{m|ang|princ|t=a wink}}: see {{l|en|prink}}.

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the verb.<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=† pry|pos=''n.''{{sup|3}}|noformat=1|id=153663|date=March 2019}}</ref>

